WEBVTT

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.010
Why?

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.630
Why does this happen?!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.510
<b>Student Council Room</b>

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.130
<b>Notice of Club Room
Use Prohibition</b>

00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.890
What's the meaning of this?

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.140
We can't grant you use of the club rooms

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.420
when you haven't formally 
registered your club.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.640
We got the six members that we need.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:11.450
We received an application for an Anime Club,

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:15.250
but it's up to us, the Student Council,

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.400
to decide whether or not the 
club can be established.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.910
Gomon-sensei, do something!

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.710
What can I do?

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.810
The principal already stamped it.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.840
I'm just a lowly teacher.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.320
You're not very dependable.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.000
And you call yourself our supervisor?

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.720
I told you not to expect much from me.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:40.250
So we're out of luck.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.610
We were just getting started, too.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.010
I think I'll go home and watch 
yesterday's late-night anime.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.430
Hey, Senpai...

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.190
Let's hit up Akiba.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.570
Akiba?

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.950
Akiba's awesome!

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.090
It's that anime Arisu-san lent me.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.080
Over there!

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.710
It's that anime you showed me, Miko-chan!

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.520
You need to calm down, Minoa.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.410
I know that it's exciting being 
in Akiba for your first time.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:18.960
All right,

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.840
I think I'll give you a lesson 
on how to enjoy Akiba.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.950
This would be a cosplay specialty shop.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.810
Is this your first time 
seeing this kind of thing?

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.670
Yes.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.360
It's amazing!

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.480
It really is just like in the anime.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.340
Cosplay is certainly important 
in discussing anime,

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.180
but there are plenty of other 
things to show an Akiba beginner.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.490
Erika-senpai?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.110
I've seen that outfit before!

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:57.130
What was it...?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.880
It's Nacchan from <i>Dub Tone</i>!

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.300
You look fantastic.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.990
They had a new one, so I had to try it out.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:07.730
That voice...

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:08.890
Erika-senpai?!

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:10.440
Yup.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.510
I couldn't tell at all.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.740
People really can't tell who you are 
once you wear a costume and a wig.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.380
Cosplayer problems.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.570
Speaking of cosplayer problems,

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.530
you know when someone wants 
to coordinate with you,

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.220
and you get all kinds of suggestions,

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.500
you go through all of them, 
and you end up sleep-deprived?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.620
Coordinate?

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.850
Cosplaying characters from the same work.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.000
I ended up checking out tons.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.630
How many?

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:48.140
I think just about everything 
that's on display here.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.510
That's amazing.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.020
If you're going to cosplay, you might as 
well get your poses down, right?

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:56.020
For that, you have to watch the anime, too.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.270
Cosplay sounds like fun.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.590
Come to think of it, you've already 
done a bunny cosplay, haven't you?

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:08.290
Hey, we don't have enough 
people to cosplay <i>Toumabu</i>.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.160
Want to try it?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.210
Huh? Me?

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.410
<i>Nakimushi Saddle</i> would work, too.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.550
I could lend you my cycling jersey.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:17.480
Um...

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.040
Don't worry.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:23.700
I'll teach you all you need to know—
poses, makeup, everything.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.050
I guess I'll give it a try, then.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.930
You've been sucked into 
Aoyama's cosplay universe.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.250
You're never getting out.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.770
<i>Saddle</i>'s great, Minoa.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.380
Next up is definitely this place.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.440
Anime Soul.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.930
It's very much the tower of dreams.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:46.390
You could also say it's a Tower of Babel, 
where lust and vices flourish.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.700
Asagaya, are you prepared to set foot?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.700
Look at this huge stack of anime magazines!

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:56.350
Aren't you guys coming in?

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:03.940
The first floor is magazines.

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.960
The second floor is new book releases.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.590
The third floor is 
previously-published books.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.720
You can get most light novels here.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:14.120
It looks like a normal bookstore so far.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.790
So far, yeah.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.480
But from the fourth floor up,

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.230
it's all anime merch!

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.310
Wow!

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.110
There's so much stuff!

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.680
They have new <i>Odopuri</i> badges.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:32.870
Badges?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.620
She means these.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.630
Oh, those badges.

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:37.860
Minoacchi.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:41.480
Don't you think these <i>Micross Gamma</i> 
rubber straps are really cute?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:46.380
So these are rubber straps?

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.850
It's such a cute SD character.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.590
I like the chibiness.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.500
It makes you collect all of them.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.890
I know.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:55.290
I love the roundness of its form.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:55.870
Yup.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:57.120
Cuteness is justice.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.270
It is.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:02.270
By the way, where did Miko go?

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.800
Kaikai's missing, too.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.210
They must have gone to the higher floors.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.570
Oh, I'll go look for them.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.660
<b>Meido</b>

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.660
Kaikai-senpai.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:20.040
Hey, Senpai?

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:31.680
An Uncertain
Magical Index

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:31.680
A Certain Report on the Irresponsible
and Depressing Chronicles of
Me and a Certain Eccentric 
Childhood Friend

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:31.680
Unlimited
Fantasy World

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.680
Y-Y-You managed to hide 
your presence from me.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.250
You're one of <i>them</i>, aren't you?

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.240
Them?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.280
I'm with the Anime Club.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.680
By the way, Kaikai-senpai...

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.450
Musashisakai Kai!

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.200
What kind of merch were you 
looking at, Kai-senpai?

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.290
Margedo Lee from <i>Higan no Arina</i>!

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.260
She's the character who wields
the evil book, Grimoire!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.070
So that's that Grim-whatever 
you were talking about.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.250
Huh?

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:55.450
But how does she fight with a book?

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:58.200
That's a good question, coming from you.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:01.330
That's where special power battles shine.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.260
Meaning?

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:05.570
Things that aren't usually used as weapons,
or abilities that aren't meant for fighting.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:09.720
Those are used in special power battles
and that's why they're interesting!

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.070
This is a book, but other examples include...

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.090
Paper,

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:15.590
coins,

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.080
electricity,

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.220
and cards!

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:21.600
Some even battle using words!

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.700
Using words?

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:25.100
I can't quite make sense of that.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:24.770
<b>Irohanihoheto</b>

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.860
That's why you're an idiot!

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.230
All right.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:32.580
Someday, I'll lend you my carefully
selected super-heated battle anime...

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:36.090
You aren't bored?

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.370
I mean, you're just listening to me.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.620
I'm excited just listening.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.630
You sure are weird.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:46.630
If I may...

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:49.050
You scared me.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:52.020
Are you aware that Margedo
Lee has a very good backstory

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:54.320
that isn't shown in the anime?

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:55.130
What?!

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:58.810
I was about to soak the book in tears.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.160
You know the truth of a 
world that I've yet to see?

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.640
You've taken a glimpse into 
the other side, have you?

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.480
I love <i>Higan no Arina</i>, after all.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:11.400
Though I prefer the original.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:16.360
The first-years this year amuse me.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:22.330
What the heck is that?

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.500
I'm so glad those two are hitting it off.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.810
Akiba's an amazing place.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.990
Sure, let's just leave it at that.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:33.300
That really was fun.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.290
Right?

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:37.180
I come here whenever I'm down.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:42.760
Hey, why don't we keep doing the Anime Club,

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.140
as an out-of-school thing?

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:46.120
Well...

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.250
I oppose.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.940
Two objections at the same time.

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.570
I-Is there a reason?

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:56.320
Because, in <i>The Club Room
and the Fish Cat's Elegant Life</i>...

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.340
...they had a club room.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:01.210
<i>The Club Room and the Fish Cat</i>?

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:04.880
It's a slice-of-life anime that focuses 
on conversations in a club room.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:08.580
I saw people online three-ep-cutting
it because it made them sleepy.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:13.410
How could they drop it 
after only three episodes?!

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:15.630
It's that chill atmosphere 
that makes it so great!

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.470
Don't tell me, tell them!

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.390
Three-ep-cutting?

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.860
They're talking about dropping 
the show after episode 3.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:27.980
Basically, they stopped watching it.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.230
Why three episodes?

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:35.930
A lot of anime has a turning 
point on the third episode.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.820
You start watching it, thinking it's 
a lighthearted magic girl anime,

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.740
when suddenly someone gets killed.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:45.160
3Kiriize Debut

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.220
They practice their songs,
work on their costumes,

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.880
and finally debut as idols!

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.250
And there isn't a single 
person in the audience.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:52.260
It's a technique used to shock the audience

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:56.230
and get them to watch the series 
until the end out of curiosity.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:59.260
In other words, if they don't 
jump the shark in episode three,

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:02.010
they're declaring that they plan 
to keep going as they were.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:03.830
Unfortunately,

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:07.520
at that point, some people will drop the 
series because it isn't their thing.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:08.770
That's way too cheap!

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:12.260
Episode three is when the background 
and setting have been presented,

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:14.520
and the story begins to really move forward.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:19.540
The characters start to build rapport, 
and their dialogue becomes more fun.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.560
It's wasteful to drop an anime
after the third episode,

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:22.860
when it's just getting started.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:23.640
Right?

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:24.830
You two are pretty close.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.920
The Anime Club's going to get the 
three-ep-cut, if we don't do something.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:36.170
It hasn't even started, so zero-ep-cut?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.520
Back to what I was saying...

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:42.310
It's when they unleash their abilities 
that a battle anime is at its best.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.970
When they unleash their abilities?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.660
For example, removing the 
bracelet from their wrist,

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.830
removing their eye patch,

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:50.710
unleashing their true powers.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.940
The catharsis is pure bliss.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.570
As for me...

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:57.400
You have one, too, Kaikai-senpai?

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.730
It's <i>Kai</i>!

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:02.120
When I remove this Witlim Opticum,

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.430
handed down to me from 
sages of generations past,

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.690
the power of my evil eye will be released,

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:09.950
and there will be hell on earth!

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:16.680
But the best part of special 
power battle anime is...

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:16.830
<i>We will soon be arriving at Ikebukuro.</i>

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.680
Hey, we're there.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:20.550
<i>Please be sure to take 
all of your belongings.</i>

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.840
Tell me more about anime sometime.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.710
<i>I wanted to hear more.</i>

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:43.360
<i>If only we had a club room, 
we could talk for a lot longer.</i>

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:58.000
<b>Notice of Emergency General Student Meeting
 in Regards to Student Council Proposal
 to Abolish the Anime Club</b>

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:03.010
<b>Erika,
Cosplayer x Cosplayer</b>

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.760
How could the student council 
abolish the Anime Club?

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.720
That's way too harsh!

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.610
Please go protest them, Gomon-sensei.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.520
I don't know, I was the one 
who brought it up, after all.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:25.470
Explain the need for an Anime Club. 
If it's approved,

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.500
it'll be given official permission 
to operate as a club.

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:31.070
Of course, we get the club room back.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:32.790
And if it's not approved?

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:34.290
Shut it down!

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:42.550
They wouldn't bite without those conditions.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.350
Besides, you were the one who 
asked me to do something about it.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.800
Come on!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.380
And so we don't get to have 
a club this year, either.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:55.550
What do you plan to do, Aoyama?

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:56.760
Nothing, really.

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:59.410
If those girls want to keep working 
at it, I'll have their back.

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:01.740
But you're not going to take any initiative?

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:05.750
That's why I suggested doing it 
as an out-of-school activity.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:08.320
That was your intention the 
whole time, too, wasn't it?

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:14.230
Erika-senpai says she won't make a speech.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.530
I figured as much.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.120
She said she wasn't particular 
about making it a club.

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:21.130
But...

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.980
<i>I wanted to hear more.</i>

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:27.660
<i>If only we had a club room,
 we could talk for a lot longer.</i>

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:33.510
I still want somewhere 
I can be with you guys.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.530
Minoa...

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:37.060
Let's protect our club room.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:39.950
Let's make the speech count.

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:40.620
Yeah.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.350
Leave the script to me.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.240
I believe in you.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.770
I know you're nervous.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.480
I am, too.

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:53.830
But the Anime Club's future 
rests on your shoulders.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:55.240
Uh...

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.410
I'll support you with everything I've got.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.980
This anime has my favorite speech.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.000
Please watch it by tomorrow.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:03.920
Right...

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.420
<b>Maoei</b>

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.420
<b>The story of the Demon King and the Hero 
who face the world of darkness hand-in-hand</b>

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:08.420
Guys, wait...

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:11.530
All right, I'm going to write 
the best speech script ever.

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:13.300
Tomorrow's the decisive battle.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.660
Me? Speech?

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:16.980
Are you all right?

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.700
Neko-senpai!

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.110
I can't make a speech!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:25.580
Here.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:28.630
It's a good luck charm.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:29.460
Keep it.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:32.700
Dried sardine?

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:38.010
Good luck, samurai girl!

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.710
I've always wanted to say that once.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:46.430
The purpose of extracurricular 
activities at this academy

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:51.090
is to enrich school life, to improve 
friendships between students,

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.750
and to thus create something meaningful.

00:15:54.750 --> 00:16:02.200
Meanwhile, watching anime is nothing 
more than unproductive pastime.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:01.790
She's just bashing anime non-stop.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:04.460
Although she's right about what she's saying.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:05.030
They immerse themselves in 
these childish, empty stories,

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:09.020
Anime is fun, but it isn't 
really creating anything.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.530
wasting huge amounts of time.

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:11.020
It is not becoming of a student.

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:10.360
Erika-senpai?

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:15.870
But whether anime has value or 
not isn't for anyone to decide.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:15.870
An extracurricular that does not 
produce any value is worthless,

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.050
and is nothing but a 
hindrance to our education.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:23.180
Therefore, I move that the 
Anime Club be abolished.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:32.080
Next, Asagaya Minoa-san of the Anime Club.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:32.880
Yes.

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.450
Minoa-chan's really tense.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:41.800
Don't worry, I gave her the best script ever.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.860
We have lost but one club room.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:48.990
Does this foreshadow our defeat?

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.650
Nay! It is a new beginning!

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:54.360
<i>Huh?</i>

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:58.160
<i>Arisu-chan told me this 
would get the crowd going.</i>

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.040
Would you <i>actually</i> use that?

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:04.290
That's supposed to be a 
perfect hook for a speech.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.710
This isn't right.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.540
Useless.

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:09.070
Um, er...

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:13.010
We of the Anime Club research anime.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.300
I mean, we don't <i>really</i> 
research anime, but...

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:16.140
Um...

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:21.350
Like, we talk about what we watched 
last night, what shows we recommend...

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:17.600
Huh?

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.300
What kind of club is that?

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.830
A light convo club?

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:21.810
Do we need that?

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:27.060
And I, well, I don't know 
anything about anime.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.640
E-Er... Um...

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:30.930
So, I...

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:32.740
But anime is...

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:53.380
When I remove my Witlim Opticum handed 
down to me from sages of generations past,

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.620
the power of my evil eye will be released,

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:59.430
and there will be hell on earth!

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:04.200
Hear me: I love special power battle anime!

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:06.440
I <i>love</i> them!

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.370
Why, you ask?

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.540
I could give you many answers.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.370
The weakest use their abilities, 
which couldn't possibly be useful in battle,

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:16.000
to make themselves into the most powerful.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:21.450
They engage in battles impossible in 
reality, razing buildings in their wake.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:23.450
It is all magnificent!

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.240
Chair! We're done, right?

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:29.980
We don't need to listen to any more of 
his arguments— I mean, his nonsense.

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:31.090
Just carry the motion to abolish...

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:31.970
Listen when I speak!

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:38.630
The best part of a special 
ability battle anime is...

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:42.590
<i>He's continuing where we left off.</i>

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.350
Is that they always side with the weak,

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:50.350
and overturn the strong but tyrannous!

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:53.170
They hear the voices of the voiceless.

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:55.360
They become power for the powerless.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.360
That is the essence of the 
special power battle anime.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:01.090
Make-believe? Convenient?

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.950
Laugh if you must.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:08.370
But it's in anime that we learned justice, 
friendship and perseverance.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:13.630
What gives the student council the 
right to declare that "worthless"?

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:17.510
This student council has not one member 
that can do an electric attack!

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.010
Not one that can teleport!

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.760
Not one with any special powers!

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:26.970
If you choose to yield to the student 
council and vote to end the Anime Club,

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.610
that is your choice to make.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:31.860
But if that's how you make your decision,
you'll be crowd characters all your lives!

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:38.710
Do you not want to become a main character, 
standing true to your beliefs?

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.280
I do!

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:44.560
For that is what anime has taught me to do.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:45.680
That is all.

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:14.270
You can't see anything without 
your glasses, can you, Kaikai?

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.790
It's <i>Kai</i>.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:20.650
I could have never done that if I could see.

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:28.570
<i>We won about half the male vote</i>

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:30.900
<i>and quite a bit of the female vote,</i>

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:33.750
<i>and we managed to reclaim the club room.</i>

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.420
<b>Club Room Usage Permission Form</b>

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.920
All right, that's that.

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:41.260
It's happening again, isn't it, Erika?

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:48.950
It's great having a club room again.

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.270
It's so relaxing.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:55.250
It's all thanks to my godly success.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.940
Now, worship me!

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:02.910
Gomon-sensei, did you 
know this would happen?

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:06.580
Well, the student council would 
have shut you down sooner or later

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.100
if you couldn't pull it off.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:08.930
Huh?

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:12.430
Apparently there have always been 
students trying to set up an Anime Club,

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:15.210
and getting shut down by the 
student council every time.

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:17.090
Why do they bother?

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.210
It's just a rumor.

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:28.720
<i>It's so nice having a club room.</i>

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.590
There's more to what makes special 
power battle anime so great.

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:35.240
It's fun to compare the show 
with the original, too.

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:37.620
We're going to train you hard!

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:38.230
Uh...

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:40.480
In that case, I've got something, too.

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:45.030
W-Wait, Arisu-chan!

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.120
I can't watch all this right away.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:48.270
Don't worry, Minoa.

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:49.730
We have the club room.

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:53.000
We have plenty of time to 
watch and discuss anime.

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:56.690
You're going to do cosplay, too, right?

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:59.010
Erika-senpai!

00:23:30.740 --> 00:23:32.300
People sometimes go,

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:35.190
"That was a good finale," 
and drop a show after episode 3.

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:37.210
Next episode: "Club Room Explosion!"

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:40.360
Watch to find out why.
